        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: conspiracy-board explainer\nTopic: tech news\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 10s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_4YZ6RYZKCXFD57JT4JJWD5GHKA",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_X6EPD07YAAJWKWAAV0ECKSCPNN",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_9875EY577D86VY43RWVQ2TMK9G",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.82,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a conspiracy-board explainer about tech news for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the conspiracy-board explainer \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a jib reveal rising over a foreground object on a 50mm anamorphic with 2x squeeze, framing with dead-centre symmetry with mirrored negative space.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with flickering firelight as the only motivated source; grade as near-monochrome with a single accent hue allowed to stay saturated. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. The response must be a lone prompt paragraph \u2014 strip any header, numbering or sign-off."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_YHXK5KXA0ZT8H6SZZ77D023N61",
